From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yash Dayani <52958495+YashDayani@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: add a network speed indicator to the status bar

Shows the current download and upload speed as a small two line
indicator in the status bar, for both Wi-Fi and mobile data, and
follows the status bar and quick settings header colors. It is off
by default. It is turned on from Settings > Network & internet (added by
the companion platform_packages_apps_Settings patch) or with:

  settings put system network_traffic_enabled 1

Further settings: network_traffic_mode (0 up and down, 1 up only,
2 down only), network_traffic_units (0 bits, 1 bytes),
network_traffic_refresh_interval (seconds), network_traffic_autohide,
network_traffic_autohide_threshold (kB/s) and network_traffic_hidearrow.

The indicator view is taken from the EvoX and crDroid SystemUI
(NetworkTraffic, Apache-2.0, crDroid Android Project) and wired into
the status bar icon pipeline of this tree. The slot is added once at
start up and the view shows or hides itself from the settings, so
PhoneStatusBarPolicy needs no extra constructor dependencies. The
switch in Settings is not part of this change.
